  "parameters": {
    "v": {
      "value": 0,
      "unit": "V",
      "conditions": {
        "t_a_c": 25
      },
      "source": {
        "note": "Zero, and deliberately not a plausible number. This entry exists to say that \"v\" is in volts, which is what the sheet needs in order to print 3.3 V rather than a bare 3.3 - a number that is a voltage, a resistance or a count depending on who is reading it. The value itself is never read: a stated point takes its voltage from the instance, and one with no instance value states nothing at all and is refused by circuit-requirement-without-value. So if this number ever does reach a wall it means that refusal has stopped working, and 0 V asked for at a divider's midpoint is wrong in a way a room sees instantly. A plausible default here would not be."
      },
      "confidence": "typical"
    }
  },
  "limits": {
    "absolute_max": {},
    "recommended": {}
  },
